## Strategic Context
This is the data layer for the dual-poll system on Expert Opinions. Poll A (Implication) opens at publish and is always available. Poll B (Retrospective) is locked until admin marks the opinion resolved.

## Acceptance Criteria

### 1. New Prisma model: ExpertOpinionVote

```prisma
model ExpertOpinionVote {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  userId    String
  user      User     @relation(fields: [userId], references: [id])
  opinionId String
  opinion   ExpertOpinion @relation(fields: [opinionId], references: [id])
  pollType  PollType
  choice    String   // BULLISH | BEARISH | NEUTRAL (IMPLICATION) or HIT | MISS (RETROSPECTIVE)
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  @@unique([userId, opinionId, pollType])
}

enum PollType {
  IMPLICATION
  RETROSPECTIVE
}
```

Add `votes ExpertOpinionVote[]` relation to the `ExpertOpinion` model.
Add `expertOpinionVotes ExpertOpinionVote[]` relation to the `User` model.
Run `npx prisma migrate dev --name add_expert_opinion_votes` from `apps/api/`.

### 2. API route: POST /api/finance/expert-opinions/[id]/vote

- Body: `{ pollType: 'IMPLICATION' | 'RETROSPECTIVE', choice: string }`
- Auth: required via `getUserIdFromRequest`. Return 401 if unauthenticated.
- Validation:
  - Opinion must exist — return 404 if not.
  - For `pollType === 'IMPLICATION'`: always allowed when opinion is PENDING.
  - For `pollType === 'RETROSPECTIVE'`: only allowed when `opinion.resolutionStatus !== 'PENDING'`. Return 400 with message 'Retrospective poll is locked until this opinion resolves' if still PENDING.
  - For IMPLICATION: valid choices are BULLISH, BEARISH, NEUTRAL.
  - For RETROSPECTIVE: valid choices are HIT, MISS.
- Operation: upsert the vote record (one per user per pollType per opinion). If user already voted, update their choice.
- Return: updated tallies object (same shape as GET /tallies).

### 3. API route: GET /api/finance/expert-opinions/[id]/tallies

- Auth: optional. When authenticated, populate `userChoice` fields from the requesting user's votes. When unauthenticated, `userChoice` is null.
- Response shape:
```typescript
{
  implication: {
    bullish: number;
    bearish: number;
    neutral: number;
    total: number;
    userChoice: 'BULLISH' | 'BEARISH' | 'NEUTRAL' | null;
  };
  retrospective: {
    hit: number;
    miss: number;
    total: number;
    userChoice: 'HIT' | 'MISS' | null;
    isLocked: boolean; // true when resolutionStatus === 'PENDING'
    unlockReason: string | null; // e.g. 'Resolved HIT on 2026-04-30' when unlocked
  };
}
```

### 4. API client methods (packages/api-client/src/index.ts)

- `castExpertOpinionVote(opinionId: string, body: { pollType: string; choice: string })` — `auth: true`, POST to `/api/finance/expert-opinions/${opinionId}/vote`
- `getExpertOpinionTallies(opinionId: string)` — `auth: true`, GET to `/api/finance/expert-opinions/${opinionId}/tallies`

### 5. New types in packages/types

```typescript
export type ApiExpertOpinionPollType = 'IMPLICATION' | 'RETROSPECTIVE';
export type ApiExpertOpinionVoteChoice = 'BULLISH' | 'BEARISH' | 'NEUTRAL' | 'HIT' | 'MISS';
export interface ApiExpertOpinionTallies {
  implication: {
    bullish: number;
    bearish: number;
    neutral: number;
    total: number;
    userChoice: 'BULLISH' | 'BEARISH' | 'NEUTRAL' | null;
  };
  retrospective: {
    hit: number;
    miss: number;
    total: number;
    userChoice: 'HIT' | 'MISS' | null;
    isLocked: boolean;
    unlockReason: string | null;
  };
}
```

### 6. Definition of Done

- `ExpertOpinionVote` model and `PollType` enum exist in schema.
- Migration committed.
- POST vote route validates pollType/choice and upserts correctly.
- Retrospective is blocked when PENDING.
- GET tallies returns correct counts and userChoice.
- api-client methods exist and typed.
- New types exported from packages/types.
- Zero TypeScript errors.

## Strategic Context
Credibility score is the trust signal that separates signal from noise in the Finance section. It is derived from crowd retrospective votes (Poll B), not from the platform team's judgment. This makes it democratic and self-reinforcing.

## Acceptance Criteria

### 1. Credibility score computation (helper function)

Create or add to `apps/api/lib/finance/credibility.ts`:

```typescript
export function computeCredibilityScore(expert: Expert & {
  opinions: Array<ExpertOpinion & {
    votes: ExpertOpinionVote[];
    resolutionStatus: string;
  }>;
}): { score: number | null; resolvedCount: number; provisional: boolean } {
  const resolved = expert.opinions.filter(
    o => o.resolutionStatus === 'RESOLVED_HIT' || o.resolutionStatus === 'RESOLVED_MISS'
  );
  const resolvedCount = resolved.length;
  if (resolvedCount < 5) return { score: null, resolvedCount, provisional: true };

  const hits = resolved.filter(opinion => {
    const retroVotes = opinion.votes.filter(v => v.pollType === 'RETROSPECTIVE');
    if (retroVotes.length === 0) return false;
    const hitCount = retroVotes.filter(v => v.choice === 'HIT').length;
    return hitCount > retroVotes.length / 2; // majority HIT
  });
  const score = hits.length / resolvedCount;
  return { score, resolvedCount, provisional: false };
}
```

This is a read-only computed value — do NOT store it in the database.

### 2. API route: GET /api/finance/experts/[id]

Create `apps/api/app/api/finance/experts/[id]/route.ts`.

Response:
```typescript
{
  id: string;
  name: string;
  organization: string;
  verified: boolean;
  bio?: string | null;
  avatarUrl?: string | null;
  credibilityScore: number | null;  // null if < 5 resolved
  provisional: boolean;             // true if < 5 resolved
  totalOpinions: number;
  resolvedCount: number;
  recentCalls: Array<{
    id: string;
    quote: string;
    direction: string;
    publishedAt: string;
    resolutionStatus: string;
    resolvedAt?: string | null;
  }>; // last 5
}
```

Fetch expert with opinions (including votes for credibility computation). Compute credibilityScore via helper. Include last 5 opinions sorted by publishedAt DESC as recentCalls.

### 3. API route: GET /api/finance/experts/[id]/calls

Create `apps/api/app/api/finance/experts/[id]/calls/route.ts`.

- Paginated list of expert's ExpertOpinion rows.
- Supports `cursor` query param.
- Each item: `{ id, quote, direction, publishedAt, resolutionStatus, resolvedAt, resolutionNote, retrospectiveTallies: { hit, miss, total } }`.
- Retrospective tallies computed from ExpertOpinionVote rows (count HIT vs MISS for RETROSPECTIVE pollType).

### 4. api-client methods

```typescript
getExpertProfile(expertId: string): Promise<ApiExpertProfile>  // GET /api/finance/experts/[id]
getExpertCalls(expertId: string, params?: { cursor?: string }): Promise<{ items: ApiExpertCall[]; nextCursor: string | null }>  // GET /api/finance/experts/[id]/calls
```

### 5. New types in packages/types

```typescript
export interface ApiExpertProfile {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  organization: string;
  verified: boolean;
  bio?: string | null;
  avatarUrl?: string | null;
  credibilityScore: number | null;
  provisional: boolean;
  totalOpinions: number;
  resolvedCount: number;
  recentCalls: ApiExpertCall[];
}

export interface ApiExpertCall {
  id: string;
  quote: string;
  direction: string;
  publishedAt: string;
  resolutionStatus: string;
  resolvedAt?: string | null;
  resolutionNote?: string | null;
  retrospectiveTallies?: { hit: number; miss: number; total: number };
}
```

### 6. Definition of Done
- `computeCredibilityScore` helper exists and handles < 5 resolved case.
- GET /api/finance/experts/[id] returns profile with computed score.
- GET /api/finance/experts/[id]/calls returns paginated calls with tallies.
- api-client methods exist and typed.
- New types exported from packages/types.
- Zero TypeScript errors.

## Strategic Context
Every expert currently shows an anonymous grey initials circle. When users see a credibility score and 'Verified' badge next to a flat-gray circle, the trust signal is undercut — it reads as a bot, not a person. Better initials + consistent verified badge across all Expert surfaces makes the credibility system feel real.

## Acceptance Criteria

### 1. Deterministic colorful initials fallback

Create a shared utility: `apps/mobile/src/utils/expertAvatar.ts`

```typescript
export function getExpertInitialsColor(name: string): string {
  // Hash the name string to one of 8 distinct accent colors.
  // Must be deterministic: same name always returns same color.
  const colors = ['#E84855', '#3A86FF', '#FF6B35', '#06D6A0', '#845EC2', '#F9C74F', '#4CC9F0', '#F72585'];
  let hash = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < name.length; i++) {
    hash = name.charCodeAt(i) + ((hash << 5) - hash);
  }
  return colors[Math.abs(hash) % colors.length];
}

export function getExpertInitials(name: string, organization: string): string {
  // Prefer first letter of name if non-empty, else first letter of organization.
  const source = name.trim() || organization.trim();
  return source.charAt(0).toUpperCase();
}
```

### 2. Apply to all Expert avatar surfaces

Replace all existing grey initials circles on:
- `apps/mobile/src/components/expert-opinion-card.tsx` — the avatar circle in the card header
- `apps/mobile/src/app/expert/[id].tsx` — the 56px header avatar
- `apps/mobile/src/app/expert-leaderboard.tsx` — each leaderboard row avatar

For each: if `expert.avatarUrl` is set, render a circular `<Image>` with `source={{ uri: expert.avatarUrl }}`. Otherwise render a colored circle (backgroundColor from `getExpertInitialsColor(expert.name || expert.organization)`) with the initials text (from `getExpertInitials`) centered inside.

### 3. Verified badge on all Expert surfaces

Add a small verified checkmark badge wherever expert name is displayed and `expert.verified === true`:
- `expert-opinion-card.tsx`: next to the expert name line. Use a small blue filled circle with a white checkmark (unicode ✓ or an icon). Size: 14px.
- `expert/[id].tsx`: already has a Verified chip — verify it is there from S16-T3 or add it.
- `expert-leaderboard.tsx`: next to the expert name in each row.

The badge should be inline with the name, not below it. Use a row with `alignItems: 'center'` and `gap: 4`.

### 4. Avatar URL in admin verification flow

When the admin uses the verify form in S17-T2, the avatarUrl they paste is saved via the POST /api/admin/experts/[id]/verify route. No additional work here — just confirm the expert profile screen and ExpertOpinionCard will render the image once the URL is set (they will, per item 2 above).

### 5. Definition of Done
- `expertAvatar.ts` utility exists with deterministic color hash.
- All 3 Expert avatar surfaces use the new colorful initials fallback (not grey).
- Verified badge present on ExpertOpinionCard, expert profile, and leaderboard rows.
- No visual regression on existing expert surfaces.
- Zero TypeScript errors.
